    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just so quiet now. i spent thirty years in operating rooms, constant adrenaline, constant purpose... every second mattered. now i just wake up, drink coffee, and stare at the wall. it feels like i'm just a ghost in a suit. there's nothing left to do, nothing left to be.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
